  "structuring": {
    "prompt_additions": "Poland uses civil law structure. Basic unit is ARTICLE (artykuł), not SECTION. Higher divisions: BOOK (księga), TITLE (tytuł), PART (dział), CHAPTER (rozdział). Subdivisions: SUBSECTION (ustęp, numbered with period: 1. 2.), POINT (punkt, numbered with right parenthesis: 1) 2)), INDENT (litera, lettered: a) b)), INDENT (tiret, unnumbered dash). Article numbering is ALWAYS continuous throughout the entire act — do not restart at each chapter. Enacting formula: 'Sejm Rzeczypospolitej Polskiej uchwala, co następuje:'"
  },
